# E338 draft: package AVR libc as a cross-target sysroot on an OHOS host

id:                     E450
trigger_tool:           conan|avr-gcc|avr-ld|avr-objdump|avr-nm
phase:                  build|package|testing
error_signature:        avr-gcc: error trying to exec 'as'|cannot find ld|cannot open linker script file|architecture: aarch64|multilib directory escapes package root|undefined reference to (memcpy|strlen|sin)

severity:               3
category:               cross-compile, sysroot-packaging, test-boundary, tool-dispatch
match_keywords:         avr-libc, OHOS host, AVR target, cross sysroot, avr-gcc -B, unprefixed as ld nm, linker scripts, multilib, weak symbol, source coverage
title:                  Keep OHOS host metadata separate from an AVR target sysroot and validate it with the target toolchain

root_cause:             avr-libc produces headers, CRT objects, linker scripts, device archives, libc and libm for the AVR target even when Conan runs on an OHOS aarch64 host. Treating those files as native Conan C library metadata lets the OHOS compiler consume incompatible paths. In addition, avr-gcc -B searches its prefix for unprefixed as, ld and nm plus avr/lib/ldscripts, so merely placing avr-prefixed binutils on PATH is insufficient.
affected_scope:         Cross-target runtime or sysroot packages built by Conan on OHOS, especially staged compiler toolchains whose compiler driver delegates to a separately packaged binutils and whose test inventory spans multilib variants.
verification_cmd:       CI_PACKAGES="archives/a/avr-libc/2.2.1" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           cross-target-resource-boundary-and-explicit-driver-dispatch
rec_description:        Model the result as a target resource package rather than an OHOS native library; keep cpp_info include, lib and libs empty; expose the sysroot through resdirs and an explicit root environment variable; construct an ephemeral avr-gcc -B dispatch root containing unprefixed binutils and linker scripts; and make test_package compile and link a real AVR ELF before checking target architecture, package-root containment and strong or weak symbol bindings.
rec_command:            conan create archives/a/avr-libc/2.2.1 --build=missing
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-cross-sysroot-resource-package

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      inventory-bounded-target-compile-link
fallback_description:   When a stage-1 compiler omits C++ or a simulator is not packaged, execute every eligible C and assembly source with a supported multilib, report executed pass rate separately from total source coverage, and list the blocked C++ and runtime inventory without claiming it passed.
fallback_command:       MCU_LIST=at90s8515 MCU_LIST_FULL=at90s8515 sh runtest.sh -c
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          explicit-eligible-test-inventory

forbid_1_pattern:       cpp_info\.(includedirs|libdirs|libs).*avr|package_type\s*=\s*"library"
forbid_1_reason:        AVR headers and archives must not be injected into an OHOS native consumer graph.
forbid_1_consequence:   The host compiler sees incompatible target headers or objects and the package boundary becomes misleading.
forbid_2_pattern:       PATH=.*avr-binutils.*avr-gcc|copy.*avr-(as|ld|nm).*PATH
forbid_2_reason:        PATH-only discovery does not satisfy avr-gcc -B lookup for unprefixed delegated tools and linker scripts.
forbid_2_consequence:   Compilation or linking fails after the compiler driver starts, despite avr-prefixed tools being present.
forbid_3_pattern:       462/462|100%.*upstream.*(?:runtime|source)
forbid_3_reason:        A C-only bootstrap compiler and no AVR simulator cannot execute the 53 C++ sources or AVR machine code.
forbid_3_consequence:   Coverage is overstated and CI evidence becomes unauditable.

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E011, E129, E206, E223]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

